---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumb from "../../components/Breadcrumb.astro";
import NameMeaning from "../../components/tools/NameMeaning.jsx";
---

<BaseLayout title="Bible Name Meanings — Discover What Biblical Names Mean" description="Search 75+ Biblical names and discover their meanings, origins, and the people behind them. Find the perfect name with spiritual significance.">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    <Breadcrumb items={[
      { name: "Home", href: "/" },
      { name: "Faith Tools", href: "/tools" },
      { name: "Bible Name Meaning", href: "/tools/name-meaning" }
    ]} />

    <div class="text-center mt-6 mb-10">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-display font-bold text-dark">
        📛 Bible Name Meaning
      </h1>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mt-3">Discover the meaning and story behind Biblical names</p>
    </div>

    <NameMeaning client:load />

    <div class="mt-12 prose prose-amber max-w-none">
      <h2 class="font-display">Why Biblical Names Matter</h2>
      <p>In the Bible, names carry deep significance. They often reflect a person's character, destiny, or the circumstances of their birth. God even changed people's names to mark turning points — Abram became Abraham ("father of many"), and Jacob became Israel ("he who struggles with God").</p>
      <h3>Popular Biblical Names Today</h3>
      <p>Many of the most popular names in the English-speaking world come from the Bible — David, Sarah, Joshua, Hannah, Matthew, and Rachel remain among the top baby names year after year. Each carries centuries of spiritual meaning and heritage.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
